#: ../../../how-to/graphics/install-nvidia-drivers.md:39
msgid "Driver versions and branches"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/graphics/install-nvidia-drivers.md:41
msgid ""
"NVIDIA drivers come with several different support life cycles, also known "
"as branches."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/graphics/install-nvidia-drivers.md:43
msgid ""
"Generally, we recommend that you install the **Production Branch** (PB) "
"drivers. These drivers are supported for one year and provide a good balance "
"of performance, latest features and stability."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/graphics/install-nvidia-drivers.md:44
msgid ""
"If you need the latest driver, such as to support a newly released game or "
"the latest CUDA APIs, you can opt for the **New Feature Branch** (NFB) "
"drivers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/graphics/install-nvidia-drivers.md:45
msgid ""
"In a regulated enterprise environment, you might prefer the **Long Term "
"Support Branch** (LTSB) drivers, which are supported for three years."
